Third-party NEURON models: downloaded, not redistributed
--------------------------------------------------------

Two of the forward models used in the paper are third-party work published on
ModelDB. Neither is included in this repository. ModelDB publishes no blanket
licence for model source; its terms ask users to cite ModelDB and the original
papers. Both models are downloaded from source by

    bash scripts/fetch_modeldb.sh

1. Wild-type and R859C Nav1.1
   ModelDB accession 87585 -- https://modeldb.science/87585
   Barela AJ, Waddy SP, Lickfett JG, et al. (2006) An epilepsy mutation in the
   sodium channel SCN1A that decreases channel excitability.
   Journal of Neuroscience 26(10):2714-2723.
   Installed into Neuron_Test/R859C/.

2. CA1 pyramidal neuron with wild-type and D212G M-current
   ModelDB accession 118986 -- https://modeldb.science/118986
   Miceli F, Soldovieri MV, Hernandez CC, Shapiro MS, Annunziato L,
   Taglialatela M (2009) Neutralization of a unique, negatively-charged residue
   in the voltage sensor of Kv7.2 subunits in a sporadic case of benign familial
   neonatal seizures. Neurobiology of Disease 34(3):501-510.
   Installed into experiments/wo6/phase2/mutant/.

ModelDB:
   McDougal RA, Morse TM, Carnevale T, et al. (2017) Twenty years of ModelDB and
   beyond: building essential modeling tools for the future of neuroscience.
   Journal of Computational Neuroscience 42(1):1-10.


Files derived from ModelDB accession 87585
------------------------------------------

Three files in Neuron_Test/R859C/ were written by modifying that entry's
APthreshold.hoc and keep its original header. They implement the paper's own
stimulus protocol and are distributed here with the original attributed above:

    neuron.hoc                 the 35-level current ladder used in the paper
    APthreshold WT-2005.hoc    threshold run, wild-type arm
    APthreshold R859C.hoc      threshold run, R859C arm

The two archived voltage traces in that directory were computed with the
mechanisms of that entry; what wrote them is not identified (docs/REPRODUCE.md).

The neuron.hoc file in each directory of pipeline/r859c/ was also written by
modifying that entry's APthreshold.hoc, keeps its original header, and is
distributed with the same attribution. Explore8's copy is identical to
Neuron_Test/R859C/neuron.hoc; the GA runs used an earlier version, and the
simulation-based-inference run a version with two added cell templates.


Differentiable Hodgkin-Huxley model
-----------------------------------

mimic_cell_activity/HH.py is an independent implementation of the Hodgkin and
Huxley (1952) equations.


Colour palette
--------------

figures/scripts/wo7_style.py uses the Okabe-Ito colour-blind-safe palette,
published as a public recommendation by Masataka Okabe and Kei Ito.
